/* book Worked example 2: Q: At 273.15 K, ice has v = 0.0010908 m³/kg and water v = 0.0010002 m³/kg, and the latent heat of fusion is 333.5 kJ/kg. Find the slope of the melting line and estimate the melting point of ice at 10 MPa.
   1. vsf = vwater − vice = 0.0010002 − 0.0010908 = −9.06 × 10⁻⁵ m³/kg.
   2. Clapeyron: dp/dT = hsf/(T·vsf) = 333 500/(273.15 × (−9.06 × 10⁻⁵)) = −1.348 × 10⁷ Pa/K.
   3. Reciprocal: dT/dp = −7.42 × 10⁻⁸ K/Pa, which is −0.0075 K per atmosphere (× 101 325 Pa).
   4. Pressure rise from 1 atm to 10 MPa: Δp = 10 000 000 − 101 325 = 9.90 × 10⁶ Pa.
   5. ΔT = −7.42 × 10⁻⁸ × 9.90 × 10⁶ = −0.73 K, so the melting point is about 273.15 − 0.73 = 272.42 K (−0.73 °C).
   Answer: The melting line has dp/dT = −1.35 × 10⁷ Pa/K; at 10 MPa ice melts at about 272.4 K, 0.73 K below the normal melting point. */
