/* book exam traps: Dropping the minus sign in κT. (∂v/∂p)T is negative, and κT must come out positive. | Mixing units in Tvβ²/κT. With κT in 1/Pa the answer is in J/(kg·K); with κT in 1/bar it is 10⁵ times too small. | Saying throttling always cools a gas. It cools only below the inversion temperature (μJT > 0); an ideal gas does not change temperature at all. | Confusing μJT = (∂T/∂p)h with (∂T/∂p)s. Throttling is at constant enthalpy, not constant entropy. */
